      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit of your 2022 F-150's automatic transmission are a serious concern, and they often point to issues within the valve body or the hydraulic control system. It's very common for these erratic readings to be caused by a malfunctioning solenoid or a worn-out pump, which can't maintain a steady pressure. You should definitely have a professional mechanic examine the transmission fluid and inspect the internal components to pinpoint the exact culprit.",
