    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the fluid looks okay though, no smell or color change. if it isnt the pump or a solenoid, could it be something else in the valve body? like debris or something blocking a passage? feels like something is just jumping around in there.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the fluid looks clean, it's certainly possible that the issue lies with debris or a blockage inside the valve body. Even if the fluid looks fine, tiny particles of metal or clutch material can get into the system, causing valves to stick or passages to restrict flow erratically. This \"jumping around\" feeling you describe is classic for a partially obstructed or sticking valve spool. It's a delicate system, so even a small piece of grit can cause major pressure fluctuations.",
      "source": "target",
